WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:03.331
- [Jim] As far as my resume,
you, you don't know me,

00:00:03.331 --> 00:00:04.930
but you know Tigger and Winnie the Pooh.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.979
[Jim as Pooh] I think it
goes something like this,

00:00:06.979 --> 00:00:10.179
but I can only do it for a
small smackerel of honey.

00:00:10.179 --> 00:00:12.209
[Jim as Tigger] And Tigger,
don't be ridicerous.

00:00:12.209 --> 00:00:13.699
Tiggers are wonderful things.

00:00:13.699 --> 00:00:15.309
Their tops are made out of rubber,

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:16.851
their bottoms are made out of springs.

00:00:16.851 --> 00:00:19.488
You gotta pay for the
rest, I'm kidding with ya.

00:00:19.488 --> 00:00:20.848
(Tigger's laugh)

00:00:20.848 --> 00:00:23.931
(light upbeat music)

00:00:28.739 --> 00:00:31.200
- [Jim] Well, you know, the
way I got into the industry,

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.309
I mean, I guess I was kind of
doing research my whole life

00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:37.811
because I'd be sitting in
the back of the classroom and

00:00:37.811 --> 00:00:40.000
(dolphin sounds) you know I thought it was

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.212
time to break out a dolphin.

00:00:41.212 --> 00:00:42.811
I, I don't wanna say
I was the class clown;

00:00:42.811 --> 00:00:45.663
I was the class wit
'cause it sounds better.

00:00:45.663 --> 00:00:48.223
Some of the characters I
played as a voice actor:

00:00:48.223 --> 00:00:49.623
[Jim as Razoul] I take my orders

00:00:49.623 --> 00:00:52.013
directly from Jafar, Princess.

00:00:52.013 --> 00:00:57.013
[Jim as Kaa] And all I want
you to do is trust in me.

00:00:57.194 --> 00:00:59.474
[Jim as Ray] The women like
a man with a big back porch

00:00:59.474 --> 00:01:01.933
some kinda yeah, whoo hoo!

00:01:01.933 --> 00:01:04.693
[Jim as Pete] Come here
you little write-off.

00:01:04.693 --> 00:01:06.314
- [Jim] People say, well,
which one's most like you?

00:01:06.314 --> 00:01:09.103
And probably Darkwing Duck
'cause he's a wise guy.

00:01:09.103 --> 00:01:10.219
[Jim As Darkwing Duck]
Well, I am the terror

00:01:10.219 --> 00:01:11.598
that flaps in the night.

00:01:11.598 --> 00:01:15.947
I am the bug that splatters
across the windshield of crime.

00:01:15.947 --> 00:01:17.530
I am Darkwing Duck.

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:20.027
[Pooh] What could be more important

00:01:20.027 --> 00:01:22.610
than a little something to eat?

00:01:23.855 --> 00:01:27.056
- [Jim] Well you know as
far as performing Pooh,

00:01:27.056 --> 00:01:28.617
You have to be true to the character;

00:01:28.617 --> 00:01:30.295
I always say that Pooh sees the world

00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:32.278
through honey-colored glasses.

00:01:32.278 --> 00:01:33.615
Not a bad way to go.

00:01:33.615 --> 00:01:34.448
(light uptempo music)

00:01:34.448 --> 00:01:38.307
- [Pooh] Somebody or
something has found my honey.

00:01:38.307 --> 00:01:40.137
- [Jim] I jokingly say
that I'm Winnie The Pooh

00:01:40.137 --> 00:01:43.507
and the anti-Pooh, 'cause
I'm the Tasmanian Devil.

00:01:43.507 --> 00:01:46.395
(wild sounds)

00:01:46.395 --> 00:01:47.667
(laughs) Taz like.

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.356
(music crescendos)

00:01:49.356 --> 00:01:53.106
- [Taz] (belligerent sounds)

00:01:54.465 --> 00:01:55.655
- [Female Tasmanian Devil]
Having a little trouble?

00:01:55.655 --> 00:01:57.667
- [Jim] A lot a times my agent
will get in touch with me,

00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:01.539
and there'll be a special
needs little boy, little girl,

00:02:01.539 --> 00:02:03.017
we're on the telephone,

00:02:03.017 --> 00:02:05.455
and they're talking to Pooh or Tigger.

00:02:05.455 --> 00:02:07.507
- [Jim As Pooh] Oh, hello there, Billy.

00:02:07.507 --> 00:02:08.497
- [Billy] How are you?

00:02:08.497 --> 00:02:09.929
- Jim as Pooh] Oh, very lovely.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.775
- [Billy] Your Tigger voice.

00:02:11.775 --> 00:02:12.977
- [Jim As Tigger] Oh, the colors,

00:02:12.977 --> 00:02:14.569
tiggers are the wonderful things,

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:16.337
their tops are made of rubber,

00:02:16.337 --> 00:02:18.358
their bottoms are made up of springs,

00:02:18.358 --> 00:02:19.267
they're bouncing,

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:21.129
- [Jim] But his response
was, it's just so cute.

00:02:21.129 --> 00:02:24.295
He's in the world, you
know Tigger was alive

00:02:24.295 --> 00:02:25.808
and talking to him.

00:02:25.808 --> 00:02:28.787
To know that you can
bring him into smileville,

00:02:28.787 --> 00:02:30.735
and where everything's happy,

00:02:30.735 --> 00:02:34.015
and you're, you know, it's
just a blessing and a half.

00:02:34.015 --> 00:02:36.078
I never take it for granted.

00:02:36.078 --> 00:02:37.987
Honestly, the most rewarding part is

00:02:37.987 --> 00:02:41.974
seeing people's reactions
and hearing stories about how

00:02:41.974 --> 00:02:45.548
this one song got them through tough times

00:02:45.548 --> 00:02:46.711
and they, they'll go back

00:02:46.711 --> 00:02:49.161
and they'll listen to "Wherever You Are"

00:02:49.161 --> 00:02:50.733
a song that Winnie the Pooh sung.

00:02:50.733 --> 00:02:52.845
- [Pooh] ♪I need you to
come here and find me ♪

00:02:52.845 --> 00:02:56.902
♪ Cause without you I'm totally lost ♪

00:02:56.902 --> 00:02:58.845
- [Jim] I'm grateful, grateful everyday.

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:02.012
(gentle upbeat music)

